    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA\n\nPart II of November 24, 2023\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 28.11.2023)\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 9'00 Postage Fee : Rs. 50'00\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nSHOP AND OFFICE EMPLOYEES (REGULATION OF EMPLOYMENT AND REMUNERATION) (AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act (Chapter 129)\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 10 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of the\n\nsection as amended is to employ before 6.00 a.m or after 6.00 p.m any female employee who has\n\nattained the age of eighteen in any institution which is engaged in business, based on information\n\ntechnology and knowledge process outsourcing or business process outsourcing or engaged in\n\nadministration of accounts or related work in a Back Office for an institute situated abroad.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 66 of the principal enactment to enable the Minister to\n\nmake regulations specifying the terms and conditions relating to welfare of such females including\n\ntheir security, transport facilities and facilities to rest to be followed by an employer who employs\n\nsuch female after 10.00 p.m. and before 6.00 a.m.\n\nClause 4 : This clause amends section 68 of the principal enactment to expand the definition of\n\nthe expression \u201coffice\u201d and is consequential to the amendment made to Clause 2.\n\nShop And Office Employees (Regulation Of Employment And Remuneration)(Amendment) L.D.-O. 27/2022\n\nAn act to amend the shop and office employees (regulation of employment and remuneration) act (chapter 129)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows: -"
