    "chunk_size_bytes": 1542,
    "chunk_text": "(3) The quorum for meetings or sittings of the Commission shall be the majority of the total number of members appointed for the time being of the Commission, which shall, in any event be not less than five members.\n\n(5) The Commission shall cause minutes of all proceedings of its meetings to be entered in records maintained for that purpose.\n\n(6) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Commission may regulate the procedure in regard to the conduct of meetings and sittings of the Commission, the transaction of business and affairs of the Commission, and subject to the law, the disciplinary procedure relating to its officers and staff.\n\nMeetings of the Commission 5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCommission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka\n\n9\n\n9. The term of the Commission shall be five years from the date of coming into operation of this Act:\n\nProvided however, the term of the Commission may be extended by the President, if the President deems such extension to be necessary, for another preiod of one year at a time, so however, the aggregate period of such extension shall not exceed two years.\n\n10. From the date of establishment and throughout its existence the Commission shall take all appropriate measures to inform the public of its existence and its objectives.\n\n11. In the performance of its functions under this Act, the Commission shall be considered an autonomous institution and shall not be subject to the control or direction of any person or authority.\n\nPART II\n\nOBJECTIVES AND MANDATE OF THE COMMISSION"
