    "chunk_text": "(zg) notwithstanding anything to the contrary in any other written law, to do all such things as necessary to achieving the objectives and mandate of the Commission.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCommission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka20\n\nPART IV\n\nREPORTS AND RECOMMENDATIONS OF THE COMMISSION\n\n15. (1) The Commission shall submit its\u2019 final report to the President at the expiration of its term containing a comprehensive account of its activities, including its recommendations.\n\n(2) The Commission shall submit interim reports bi-annually with recommendations prior to the submission of its final report, following a sustained period of investigations, at least annually, detailing the work of the Commission. Such Interim Reports shall be submitted to the President.\n\n(3) Immediately upon submitting the final report and such interim reports as provided for under subsections (1) and (2) to the President, the Commission shall publish all such reports, using print and electronic media, including social media, and shall make copies of the reports or summaries thereof, widely available to the public in Sinhala, Tamil and English languages. The Commission shall ensure wide publicity for its recommendations, by involving inter alia, the media.\n\n(4) Within twenty-one days from the date of receipt of an interim report or the final report of the Commission in terms of subsections (1) and (2), the President shall have such reports tabled in Parliament.\n\n(5) The final report of the Commission shall include -\n\n(a) root causes of the alleged damage or harm caused\n\nAll persons shall co-operate with the Commission\n\nReports of the Commission\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCommission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka\n\n21\n\nto persons or property or loss of life, described in section 12;\n\n(b) observations of the Commission on alleged damage or harm or loss of life caused to persons or property 