    "chunk_text": "25. The Commission shall have a Secretariat which shall be charged with the responsibility for the administration of the affairs of the Commission. The Secretariat shall include, the Victim and Witness Protection Division and the Data Management Division and such other division as the Commission may consider necessary.\n\n(2) The President may, in consultation with the Commission, remove the Director General for good cause.\n\n(3) The Director General shall be responsible for the management and administration of the business and affairs\n\nDuty to inform people of their rights and potential use of their information\n\nDuty to ensure the rights of aggrieved persons, and any other person without discrimination\n\nSecretariat\n\nDirector General\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCommission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka\n\n25\n\nof the Commission, including but not limited to the following functions\u2013\n\n(a) day to day management and administration of the business and affairs of the Commission;\n\n(b) maintaining custody and preservation of all records, documents and materials of the Commission;\n\n(c) management of the assets of the Commission; and (d) performance of such other duties as may be assigned by the Commission from time to time.\n\n27. (1) All divisions of the Secretariat, unless otherwise provided for by the Commission, shall be under the purview of the Director General of the Commission.\n\n(2) All officers and staff of such divisions shall be appointed by the Commission, and shall be full-time employees of the Commission, unless otherwise decided by the Director General and approved by the Commission.\n\n(3) All such officers and staff shall be removed by the Commission only for good cause.\n\n(4) The officers and staff of all such divisions shall reflect the pluralistic nature of Sri Lanka, including gender."
