    "chunk_size_bytes": 1991,
    "chunk_text": "(4) The appointed date shall be a date not later than aperiod of six months from the date on which the provisionsof this section come into operation.\n\n2. This Act shall apply to the following entities: -\n\n(b) statutory funds and trusts to which public financeis allocated with the approval of the Parliament;\n\nShort titleand date ofoperation\n\nApplicationof this Act\n\n20\n\n2Public Debt Management\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nEstablishmentof the PublicDebtManagementOffice ofSri Lanka\n\n(c)State-owned enterprises;\n\n(d)Provincial Councils, Ministries, Departments, otherinstitutions coming under the Provincial Councilsand local authorities; and\n\n(e)any other entity.\n\n3. Public debt management is the process of establishingand executing a medium to long term strategy for managingpublic debt with the following objectives:\u2013\n\n(a)to meet financing needs and debt paymentobligations on a timely basis;\n\n(b)to borrow at the lowest costs as possible over themedium to long term, consistent with a prudentdegree of risk; and\n\n(c)to promote the development of the domestic debtsecurities market.\n\nPART I\n\nESTABLISHMENT OF THE PUBLIC DEBT MANAGEMENT OFFICE\n\n4. There shall be established an office called the PublicDebt Management Office (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cOffice\u201d) within the Ministry of Finance which shall beresponsible for the \u2013\n\n(a)management of the debt of the Government;\n\n(b) issuance and management of loan guarantees;\n\n(c)management of on-lending operations; and\n\n(d)recording and reporting of public debt.\n\nPublic debtmanagementobjectives\n\n3Public Debt Management\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n5. (1) There shall be a Director-General appointed by theCabinet of Ministers.\n\n(2) The Director-General shall be the head of the Officeand be responsible for the overall operations of the Office.\n\n(3) The terms and conditions of employment includingremuneration for all employees of the Office shall bedetermined by the prevailing Government regulations asmay be applicable from time to time."
