    "chunk_text": "sections 27, 55, 60 and 71A of the principal enactment.\n\n1Civil Procedure Code (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nShort title\n\nAmendmentof section 5of Chapter101\n\nL.D.-O. 72/2021\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CIVIL PROCEDURE CODE (CHAPTER 101)\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Civil Procedure Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2024.\n\n2. Section 5 of the Civil Procedure Code (Chapter 101)(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended by the insertion immediately after the definitionof the expression \u201cdecree\u201d, of the following new definition:-\n\n\u201c\u201celectronic\u201d shall have the same meaning assigned toit by the Electronic Transactions Act, No.19 of2006;\u201d.\n\n3. Section 9 of the principal enactment is hereby amendedby the repeal of paragraph (a) thereof, and the substitutiontherefor of the following new paragraph: -\n\n\u201c(a) a party plaintiff or a party defendant resides; or\u201d.\n\n4. Section 27 of the principal enactment is hereby amendedas follows: -\n\n(1) in subsection (1) thereof-\n\n(a)in paragraph (b) by the substitution, for the words\u201cparty whom he represents; and\u201d, of the words \u201cpartywhom he represents;\u201d; and\n\n(b)by the repeal of paragraph (c) thereof, and thesubstitution therefor of the following newparagraphs: -\n\nAmendmentof section 9of theprincipalenactment\n\nAmendmentof section 27of theprincipalenactment\n\nCivil Procedure Code (Amendment)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n\u201c(c)include an electronic mail address and amobile phone number to which service of anyprocess, notice or any other legal documentsmay also be served on a registered attorney;"
