    "chunk_text": "2. (1) The Anti-Dumping and Countervailing Duties Act,No. 2 of 2018 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipalenactment\u201d) is hereby amended by the substitution for thewords \u201cDirector-General\u201d and \u201cDepartment\u201d wherever thosewords occur in the principal enactment, of the words\u201cSecretary\u201d and \u201cOIT\u201d respectively.\n\n3. Section 85 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows: -\n\n(1)by the repeal of the definition of the expression\u201cDepartment\u201d and \u201cDirector-General\u201d;\n\n(2)by the repeal of the definition of the expression\u201cMinister\u201d and the substitution therefor of thefollowing :-\n\nShort title\n\n10\n\n15\n\nAmendmentof Act, No. 2of 2018\n\n20Amendmentof section 85of theprincipalenactment\n\n25\n\n2Anti-Dumping and CountervailingDuties (Amendment)\n\n\u201c\u201cMinister\u201d means the Minister assigned thesubject of International Trade;\u201d;\n\n(3)by the insertion of new definition of expressionimmediately after the definition of the expression\u201cnon-actionable subsidy\u201d, of the following: -\n\n\u201c\u201cOIT\u201d means the Office for International Tradeestablished under section 99 of the of theEconomic Transformation Act, No. of2024;\u201d; and\n\n(4)by the insertion of the following new definitionimmediately after the definition of the expression\u201cprovisional measures\u201d:-\n\n\u201c\u201cSecretary\u201d means the Secretary to the Ministryof the Minister assigned the subject ofInternational Trade;\u201d.\n\n4. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency\n\nAnti-Dumping and CountervailingDuties (Amendment)3\n\nDepartment of Government Printing"
