    "chunk_size_bytes": 2010,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore, enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Isiwara Development,Social Services and Charity Foundation (Incorporation)Act, No. of 2024.\n\nShort title\n\nPreamble\n\n25\n\nIncorporationof the IsiwaraDevelopment,SocialServices andCharityFoundation\n\n2Isiwara Development, Social Services and CharityFoundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n3. The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014\n\n(a) to provide medical aid and food to the poor and thedestitute and constucting houses and shelters;\n\n(b) to conduct special services for needy school childrenand to offer assistance by way of scholarships, libraryfacilities and other necessary support for students;\n\n(c) to conduct classes for the students sitting for yearfive scholarship, GCE (O/L) and GCE (A/L)examinations by experts in the particular field ofeducation;\n\n(d) to establish and maintain pre-schools for earlychildhood development of the needy children;\n\n(e) to give aid by way of scholarships to any officer orservants engaged in the furtherance of the objects ofthe Corporation;\n\n(f) to promote understanding, co-operation andfriendship with similar institutions within andoutside Sri Lanka;\n\n(g) to organize employees of small and medium scaleindustries and enterprises and working towards theirfuture advancement;\n\n(h) to design and implement social mobilizationprogrammes for the development of children andwomen and implementing education and trainingprogrammes for this purpose;25\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation\n\nIsiwara Development, Social Services and CharityFoundation (Incorporation)3\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(i) to initiate and implement technical, industrial andcomputer vocational training institutions andprogrammes so that young men and women fromfamilies of low social status can gain self employmentopportunities ;\n\n(j) to provide assitance in times of natural anddisasters, emergencies and accidents ;"
  },
